@*
    A Project's face (ADR-0083): the shared AgentAvatar drawn as a square with sharp corners, so a Project never reads as its Team
    (a rounded square) or as a person (a circle). It is a thin wrapper, as TeamAvatar is: the label-then-monogram precedence and the
    colours stay in AgentAvatar. A Project's avatar is initials or a short label (an emoji) and never a picture, and it is drawn a
    size below its Team's wherever the two meet: 24px in the sidebar beside the Team card's 40px, and 24px in the Project page
    header where the Team page's is 32px. It is read from ITeamCatalog (Find(team)?.ProjectAvatar(project)); its fields live in
    the Project folder's _project.md.
*@
@using Agency.Huddle.App.Avatars

<AgentAvatar Name="@this.Project" Avatar="this.Avatar" Size="this.Size" Class="@this.Class" Shape="AvatarShape.Square" />

@code {
    /// <summary>The Project's name, the source of the monogram fallback.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    [EditorRequired]
    public string Project { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>The Project's avatar, or <see langword="null"/> for none, which draws the monogram of the name.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Avatar? Avatar { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The avatar's size; <see cref="MudBlazor.Size.Small"/> (24px) by default, a size below a Team's.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Size Size { get; set; } = Size.Small;

    /// <summary>Extra CSS classes for the root avatar.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Class { get; set; }
}
